High in the west front of a Gothic cathedral, a great circular window of
stained glass catches the afternoon sun and throws colored light across the
stone floor. The rose window is the European mandala: a centered, radial design
of glass and tracery, built at architectural scale.

## The wheel of light

Rose windows are organized exactly like mandalas elsewhere: a center, radial
symmetry, concentric rings, an outer boundary. The center often holds Christ or
the Virgin; the rings carry prophets, saints, and scenes arranged around the
middle.

## A mandala you stand inside

Unlike a painted mandala, the rose window surrounds the worshipper. The light
itself, shifting through the day, becomes part of the contemplative effect.

